TUnit uses `[Before(…)]` and `[After(…)]` attributes with a `HookType` enum to control scope. Here's a sketch for each:

## 1. Before/After Every Test (method-level)

```csharp
public class DatabaseTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase()
    {
        // runs before each [Test] in this class
        InMemoryDb.Reset();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // runs after each [Test]
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Query_ReturnsExpected() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once Per Class (class-level)

```csharp
public class FixtureTests
{
    private static ServiceFixture _fixture = null!;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenFixture()
    {
        _fixture = new ServiceFixture();
        _fixture.Start();
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture()
    {
        _fixture.Dispose();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task ServiceIsReachable() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> Class-level hooks **must be `static`**.

## 3. Once Per Assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock()
    {
        WireMockServer.Start();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock()
    {
        WireMockServer.Stop();
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it by the attribute.

## 4. Once Per Test Session (global)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseMigration
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations()
    {
        EfCoreMigrator.MigrateUp();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDown()
    {
        EfCoreMigrator.DropDatabase();
    }
}
```

`TestSession` spans the entire process — it fires once before any assembly runs and once after all are done.

---

### Summary table

| Scope | Attribute | Must be static? |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | No |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | Yes |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | Yes |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | Yes |

All hooks can be `async Task` if needed. The `HookType` values (`Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, `TestSession`) are imported via `using static TUnit.Core.HookType;` or fully qualified.
